{"/api/discogs/artist/2275914/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2275914","image":"https://i.discogs.com/g3gimw_ZG4YyJY6QbSm99-inv0KJFBUmekHtrM3wrlg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:408/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyNzU5/MTQtMTUwMjg2NjM1/Mi01Mzk2LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/fiHwXy3PVBQ8hPvg8o3edO9lGXr1eHYp8-3jV56rSZ8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyNzU5/MTQtMTUwMjg2NjM1/Mi01Mzk2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Taiwanese band","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2275914","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":4460216,"name":"伍佰"},{"active":true,"id":5571118,"name":"朱劍輝"},{"active":true,"id":5792475,"name":"Dino Zavolta"},{"active":true,"id":5792478,"name":"余大豪"},{"active":true,"id":13034238,"name":"China Blue (10)"}],"namevariations":["CH Blue","China Blue","Wu Bai & China Blue","Wu Bai And China Blue","伍佰","伍佰 + China Blue","伍佰 And China Blue","伍佰 and China Blue","伍佰/China Blue"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2275914-伍佰-China-Blue","type":"artist","urls":["http://wubai.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/387/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"387","image":"https://i.discogs.com/a4Mh64UZSVZ-NbQDVdBn0xghv3_-TjH9tASyOaMXMC8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:516/w:523/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM4Ny0x/NTkzNDUxOTY3LTE3/MTYuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/ZZ7yqJnX-pyGUL2dsJgCavN3r4rD6_vYBOVi0Kj8Q1U/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM4Ny0x/NTkzNDUxOTY3LTE3/MTYuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"This prolific artist has been producing breakbeat, jungle, and drum and bass since the early 90s. The \"Mutant Jazz\" single and the critically acclaimed album \"Self Evident Truth Of An Intuitive Mind\" (both released in 1995) are touted as staple Drum and Bass classics.\r\n\r\nIn 1998, T Power, along with Cris Stevens, formed \"Chocolate Weasel\" and released the single \"Music for Body Lockers\", followed by a funk and hip-hop album called \"Spaghettification\".\r\n\r\nT Power also collaborated with Shy FX (Andre Williams), both as Ebony Dubsters and Shy FX and T Power.  The duo's 2001 breakthrough track \"Shake Ur Body\" with vocalist Di reached Number 7 hit in the UK Singles Chart.  Released on EMI subsidiary Positiva, it gained widespread support from both club and commercial radio DJs and helped to further popularize drum & bass as a mainstream music genre.  The success of \"Shake Ur Body\" was followed by the duo's album \"Set It Off\", released in 2002 on Pete Tong's label F.F.R.R.. Several EPs and single releases followed; by 2005, Shy FX had made the decision to consolidate his releases onto his own label and founded Digital Soundboy Recordings. In collaboration with T Power, they subsequently released the album Diary of a Digital Sound Boy on 17 October 2005, featuring the songs \"Feelings\", \"On The Run\" and \"Plastic Soul\". Shy FX and T Power also released \"Don't Wanna Know\" featuring Di and MC Skibadee. The song was notably used on the UK television programme Soccer AM as part of the 'Skills Skool' feature.\r\n\r\nIn 2009, T Power reincarnated himself as Mr. Sofalumpkins, an electro/breakbeat/techno DJ, performing live Ableton sets, which consisted of a new sound and original new tracks.\r\n\r\nIn 2013, T Power collaborated with John Rolodex on the single, \"That Jungle Vibe - Featuring Khadija\", which was released on V Records.\r\n\r\nIn 2014, T Power released \"The Lazy Nine\", his first album under his own name Marc Royal, on Adastra Recordings (his own record label).\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:387","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":3582,"name":"Atomic Dog"},{"id":17562,"name":"Auto Maton"},{"id":368506,"name":"Marc Royal"},{"id":2000529,"name":"Mr Sofalumpkins"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["T - Power","T Power","T- Power","T-Power","T. Power","T>Power","TPower","Tea Power","T·Power"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/387-TPower","type":"artist","urls":["https://tpower.bandcamp.com/","https://www.facebook.com/pages/T-Power/273539285034?ref=hl"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5049380/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5049380","image":"https://i.discogs.com/7z5QBaPSLzsxQFQWTQvAfmsdZVapM_u0feX-KCGStmA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:574/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUwNDkz/ODAtMTU5OTY4MjU0/Mi0yMzk4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/CE4DzgMiq0ZgvlgqCmVjLEKHYRqr1f1SZteFhiJ3U5E/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUwNDkz/ODAtMTU5OTY4MjU0/Mi0yMzk4LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Producer from Plaistow, East London.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5049380","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":5342529,"name":"Joe Baker (13)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["FDW","Forrest Drive West"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5049380-Forest-Drive-West","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/ForestDriveWest/","https://soundcloud.com/forest-drive-west","https://forestdrivewest.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5377444/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5377444","image":"https://i.discogs.com/_bNJZmpBBSIPBfG084Tapi7LfZX-STep62_0zNtrZ08/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:503/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUzNzc0/NDQtMTYzMjU2NDcz/Ny00OTAxLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/3H9VnRmpl_DtCFQv71LPzgP2Li3h_0x0NQx01wJBjog/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUzNzc0/NDQtMTYzMjU2NDcz/Ny00OTAxLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Electronic music producer from Malmö Sweden based in Barcelona, Spain\r\n\r\nArmand began making music in Edinburgh at the suggestion of a respected friend. He spent time experimenting with music and exploring the possibilities contained within his laptop was cathartic relief from the grind of finishing his studies. Later returning to his hometown of Malmö, his interest in making music would intensify thanks to encouragement from his old school friends and a the looming spectre of a 9-5 lifestyle. A move to Barcelona and the end of a relationship resulted in extended sessions watching the classic American sitcom and the music made to reflect that appeared under the name DJ Seinfeld.\r\n\r\nHe initially started DJ Seinfeld as a temporary side project, but it took on a life of its own toward the end of 2016, when the Season 1 EP was released by Lobster Theremin. The release's meme-like artwork and the jokey-sounding moniker combined with track titles like \"Feel de Bum Slap\" caused many observers to question the artist's authenticity, and he was frequently lumped in with producers like Ross from Friends and the Winona Ryder-sampling DJ Boring as part of an ironic \"lo-fi house\" craze. Regardless, the media attention helped boost his career, and additional Seinfeld 12\"s were released by Natural Sciences, E-Beamz, and Endotherm in 2017, with debut full-length Time Spent Away from U appearing on Lobster Fury in November.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5377444","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":5143206,"name":"Armand Jakobsson"},{"id":5143207,"name":"Rimbaudian"},{"id":5685531,"name":"Birds Of Sweden"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5377444-DJ-Seinfeld","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/dj-seinfeld","https://djseinfeld.bandcamp.com","https://www.facebook.com/djseinfeld/","https://www.instagram.com/dj_seinfeld/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5648334/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5648334","image":"https://i.discogs.com/xj3GJ7veXxo10-K9hB0aFl3qF-M8RuFEkhRZv30oadw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU2NDgz/MzQtMTc5MDYzNjg1/NC02MDQ1LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/H_tAuIwa9-cfPjbBlJTVoKZjRuntMq5KZCeC-NLOkAU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU2NDgz/MzQtMTc5MDYzNjg1/NC02MDQ1LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Rosalia Vila Tobella (born 25 September 1992, in Sant Cugat del Vallès, Barcelona), known mononymously as Rosalía, is a Spanish singer, songwriter, producer, actress and musician.\r\nShe has become known for her modern approach of flamenco music and for her genre-bending musical styles, evolving from folk to the mainstream and avant-pop.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5648334","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":7123404,"name":"Rosalía Vila Tobella"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["ROSALÍA","Rosalia","Rosalía","ロザリア"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5648334-Rosalía-3","type":"artist","urls":["https://rosalia.com/","https://open.spotify.com/artist/7ltDVBr6mKbRvohxheJ9h1?autoplay=true&v=A","https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCQt9awGIFZeldFsATZNeJag","https://twitter.com/rosalia","https://www.instagram.com/rosalia.vt/","https://www.instagram.com/holamotomami/","https://www.facebook.com/musicarosaliabarcelona/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosal%C3%ADa_Vila","https://www.tiktok.com/@rosalia?lang=es","https://www.setlist.fm/setlists/rosalia-13c3511d.html","https://www.rosaliabarcelona.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/60606/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"60606","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"Clyde, is a Derby original. In his teens he was in several local bands, and it's noteworthy that as part of The Underdogs he supported UK chart toppers Dr & the Medics (The Underdogs were much better, even if Clyde's axe was feeding back like a mutha fu**a). Clyde also played an integral role in the setting up of Mantis Recordings, and remixed Atjazz on the first ever release. He made further musical ripples with his remix of Mikeal Fitzpatrick's ‘Wish' on Yellow Productions, and appeared on Mantis again, this time with a shadowy and anxious mix of Kimbu Kimra's ‘Raise the Dead'. \r\n\r\nAfter spending years trying to convince Clyde to give the world more of his distinct style of music, Mantis finally persuaded him to write an album, by bribing him with food and breasts. The debut single 'Serve it Up' featured San Francisco-based rapper Capitol A who's flowing rhymes told a familiar tale of a night out at the club. It certainly struck a chord with many dancefloors, both musically and lyrically, spawning many tracks in a similar vein to hit the club soundsystems. \r\n\r\nThe debut Clyde album ‘Hyper Reality' is now at long last completed, Capitol A once more stepping to the mic on several tracks including the second single ‘Broken Slang'. Clyde himself has also flexed his own vocal stylings on the album. His voice may be familiar to those who've recently heard Brooks, as Clyde co-wrote and sung tracks on his second album, Red Tape. He is also writing and singing with Rhythm Plate and Atjazz for forthcoming releases. \r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:60606","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":507950,"name":"Clive Astin"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Clive Astin"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/60606-Clyde","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.instagram.com/clyde_beats/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/8763772/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"8763772","image":"https://i.discogs.com/8mtQlPFE2zhPoIHgniCzKo7GhDp9eSXSt4sdmpAdfEo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:481/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTg3NjM3/NzItMTY3MTgyNjk5/Mi03MjUxLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/VFbxIhjpnczu4Y9BC-il1QfkXYWQWj7aIEXXbBwY7jc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTg3NjM3/NzItMTY3MTgyNjk5/Mi03MjUxLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Se Dice Guango","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:8763772","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":7735068,"name":"Manuel Printzen"},{"id":7735983,"name":"Robobok"},{"id":8437653,"name":"DJ Panam"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":7735190,"name":"DJs Winning Eleven"},{"active":true,"id":12267316,"name":"Gorducci GanG"}],"m