:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTE2Mzc2/ODctMTU2NDE3NDE4/Mi02MjUxLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/uswHZiAi3x93Ka9JxjER5IrMCJY0RRzHU5Y-drJ5d7w/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTE2Mzc2/ODctMTU2NDE3NDE4/Mi02MjUxLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"UK label founded by [a866374] ([a658057]).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1637687","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1637687-Ancient-Astronauts","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/314/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"314","image":"https://i.discogs.com/AhDYfFiChG56d8GoNDDgHuWhkW-hi8P7sFAEkbYsx3c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTMxNC0x/NzQwMDU5MjM4LTE1/NDguanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/YcRBGM11TI3fv_PdrMSMWs9aabCwo-Ug0lxlSOvigkY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTMxNC0x/NzQwMDU5MjM4LTE1/NDguanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"House music label from Chicago, Illinois, founded by [a=Jesse Saunders] in 1985. \r\n\r\nStarted off as Dance Mania Records before later (in 1988) changing name to just [b]Dance Mania[/b] and later still to [l=Dance Mania Inc.] Jesse conveyed Dance Mania in 1986 to [a=Raymond Barney] when he left for Los Angeles.  The label became known for raw, percussive tracks from the very beginning. Early hits included [a=Lil' Louis] \"Video Clash\", \"How I Feel\", \"War Games\", \"7 Ways\" by [a=Hercules], and perhaps the most known classic, \"Housenation\" by [a=The Housemaster Boyz] in 1986. Ray's own company, [l=Barney's Records], distributed many of the early Chi-labels, like [l=G Strings], [l=Chicago Underground], [l=Warehouse Records (2)], etc. \r\n\r\nIn the period of 1992-1993 Dance Mania began to release records from new the breed of Chicago artists, namely from the likes of: [a=DJ Funk], [a=Paul Johnson], [a=Eric Martin], [a=Traxmen], [a=Parris Mitchell], [a=DJ Deeon], [a=DJ Milton] and more. Label returned to it's roots, to the dirty side of disco that was always very popular in Chicago. In few years it released around 200 records, making the matrix number rise close to \"DM300\". \r\n\r\n[a=DJ Funk] bought the website DanceManiaRecords.com. \r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:314","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":1518528,"name":"Dancemania Records (2)"},"sublabels":[{"id":163742,"name":"Dance Mania Digital"},{"id":211818,"name":"Subterranean Playhouse LLC."},{"id":5868,"name":"Subterranean Playhouse Series"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/314-Dance-Mania","type":"label","urls":["http://dancemaniarecords.com","http://www.facebook.com/DanceManiaRecords","http://www.myspace.com/dance_mania_records","https://web.archive.org/web/20150127050616/http://dancemaniarecordsusa.com/about.html"]}},"/api/discogs/label/957753/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"957753","image":"https://i.discogs.com/DnHjkqQ03AJQjI40OfzfEBZUjjI1GSXI_EXanOzoyRw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTk1Nzc1/My0xNDUzODAzMjgz/LTMxNTguanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/HXcnJyExziBt9-2COQ_n8tavkJ7wS0Xv0fD8_CGLDos/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTk1Nzc1/My0xNDUzODAzMjgz/LTMxNTguanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"What good is a journey without a great soundtrack to match? This is exactly the thought that Albert had. He loved to provide music for his family as they ventured on their summer holidays. So with a few days to go they would gather the records they’d amassed over the year and copy their favourite tunes to tape. Ready to start the car, pile in, pop the tape, entitled \"Albert's Favourites\", in the player and head off. Today Albert’s Favourites is a south London studio, production family and label founded by Albert's grandson Adam [a=Scrimshire] with [a=Jonny Drop] and Dave Koor of [a=The Expansions]. Home to several collab